{
  "title": "Worker Pod JVM",
  "uid": "jmeterJvm",
  "description": "Both JVMs inside each worker pod, side by side: (left) the local-orchestrator process that tails the JTL and streams metrics to Kafka, and (right) the JMeter child process that generates load. Orchestrator series come from Spring Boot actuator (jvm_memory_*, jvm_threads_*, process_cpu_usage). JMeter-child series come from the orchestrator's JmxMetricsCollector, re-published as jmeter_jvm_* Micrometer gauges on the same /actuator/prometheus endpoint (so both carry role=localOrchestrator + the same instance label). JMeter panels show 'No data' between runs — the child only exists while a test is running. Source: each worker pod's /actuator/prometheus, discovered via Prometheus docker_sd_config (label com.perf.jmeterCloud.role=local-orchestrator). The Pod dropdown is empty until at least one worker is spawned.",
  "tags": ["jmetercloud", "jvm", "worker"],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 5,
  "refresh": "30s",
  "time": { "from": "now-30m", "to": "now" },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "pod",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": "Prometheus",
        "label": "Pod",
        "query": "label_values(jvm_memory_used_bytes{role=\"localOrchestrator\"}, instance)",
        "refresh": 2,
        "includeAll": true,
        "multi": true,
        "current": { "text": "All", "value": "$__all" },
        "sort": 1
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "gauge",
      "title": "Orchestrator heap used %",
      "description": "Orchestrator heap occupancy = used / max (-Xmx). Sustained > 85% means the 1g orchestrator heap is under pressure.",
      "gridPos": { "x": 0, "y": 0, "w": 6, "h": 5 },
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "100 * sum(jvm_memory_used_bytes{role=\"localOrchestrator\",area=\"heap\",instance=~\"$pod\"}) / sum(jvm_memory_max_bytes{role=\"localOrchestrator\",area=\"heap\",instance=~\"$pod\"})"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent", "min": 0, "max": 100,
          "thresholds": { "mode": "absolute", "steps": [
            { "color": "green", "value": null },
            { "color": "yellow", "value": 70 },
            { "color": "red", "value": 85 }
          ] }
        }
      },
      "options": { "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"] }, "showThresholdLabels": false, "showThresholdMarkers": true }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "gauge",
      "title": "JMeter child heap used %",
      "description": "JMeter child heap occupancy = used / max (-Xmx 2g). Sustained > 85% means the load generator is heap-starved — raise JMETER_JVM_ARGS / the worker container limit. 'No data' between runs is expected.",
      "gridPos": { "x": 6, "y": 0, "w": 6, "h": 5 },
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "100 * sum(jmeter_jvm_heap_used_bytes{role=\"localOrchestrator\",instance=~\"$pod\"}) / sum(jmeter_jvm_heap_max_bytes{role=\"localOrchestrator\",instance=~\"$pod\"})"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent", "min": 0, "max": 100,
          "thresholds": { "mode": "absolute", "steps": [
            { "color": "green", "value": null },
            { "color": "yellow", "value": 70 },
            { "color": "red", "value": 85 }
          ] }
        }
      },
      "options": { "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"] }, "showThresholdLabels": false, "showThresholdMarkers": true }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Orchestrator -Xmx (per pod)",
      "description": "jvm_memory_max_bytes heap ceiling — should read ~1 GiB.",
      "gridPos": { "x": 12, "y": 0, "w": 6, "h": 5 },
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "max(jvm_memory_max_bytes{role=\"localOrchestrator\",area=\"heap\",instance=~\"$pod\"})"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "bytes" } },
      "options": { "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"] }, "colorMode": "value", "graphMode": "none" }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "JMeter child -Xmx (per pod)",
      "description": "jmeter_jvm_heap_max_bytes — should read ~2 GiB once a run is active (proves the heap bump landed). 'No data' between runs.",
      "gridPos": { "x": 18, "y": 0, "w": 6, "h": 5 },
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "max(jmeter_jvm_heap_max_bytes{role=\"localOrchestrator\",instance=~\"$pod\"})"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "bytes" } },
      "options": { "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"] }, "colorMode": "value", "graphMode": "none" }
    },

    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Orchestrator — heap used vs committed vs max",
      "description": "Used approaching max = GC pressure; committed approaching max = JVM won't release pages to the OS. The flat 'max' line is -Xmx (1g).",
      "gridPos": { "x": 0, "y": 5, "w": 12, "h": 9 },
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "maxDataPoints": 500,
      "targets": [
        { "refId": "A", "expr": "sum by (instance) (jvm_memory_used_bytes{role=\"localOrchestrator\",area=\"heap\",instance=~\"$pod\"})", "legendFormat": "{{instance}} used" },
        { "refId": "B", "expr": "sum by (instance) (jvm_memory_committed_bytes{role=\"localOrchestrator\",area=\"heap\",instance=~\"$pod\"})", "legendFormat": "{{instance}} committed" },
        { "refId": "C", "expr": "sum by (instance) (jvm_memory_max_bytes{role=\"localOrchestrator\",area=\"heap\",instance=~\"$pod\"})", "legendFormat": "{{instance}} max (Xmx)" }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "bytes", "custom": { "axisLabel": "Heap (bytes)" } } },
      "options": { "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }, "legend": { "displayMode": "table", "placement": "bottom", "calcs": ["mean", "max", "lastNotNull"] } }
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "JMeter child — heap used vs max",
      "description": "jmeter_jvm_heap_used_bytes vs jmeter_jvm_heap_max_bytes (-Xmx 2g). Used riding the max line over a long run = the JMeter heap is the bottleneck. 'No data' between runs.",
      "gridPos": { "x": 12, "y": 5, "w": 12, "h": 9 },
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "maxDataPoints": 500,
      "targets": [
        { "refId": "A", "expr": "sum by (instance) (jmeter_jvm_heap_used_bytes{role=\"localOrchestrator\",instance=~\"$pod\"})", "legendFormat": "{{instance}} used" },
        { "refId": "B", "expr": "sum by (instance) (jmeter_jvm_heap_max_bytes{role=\"localOrchestrator\",instance=~\"$pod\"})", "legendFormat": "{{instance}} max (Xmx)" }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "bytes", "custom": { "axisLabel": "Heap (bytes)" } } },
      "options": { "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }, "legend": { "displayMode": "table", "placement": "bottom", "calcs": ["mean", "max", "lastNotNull"] } }
    },

    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Orchestrator — GC pause time (rate)",
      "description": "rate(jvm_gc_pause_seconds_sum) = stop-the-world GC pause seconds per second, split by action/cause. The ~5-min G1 'G1 Old Generation' blips are normal as long as pauses stay short and heap returns to baseline.",
      "gridPos": { "x": 0, "y": 14, "w": 12, "h": 8 },
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "maxDataPoints": 500,
      "targets": [
        { "refId": "A", "expr": "sum by (instance, action, cause) (rate(jvm_gc_pause_seconds_sum{role=\"localOrchestrator\",instance=~\"$pod\"}[$__rate_interval]))", "legendFormat": "{{instance}} {{action}} ({{cause}})" }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "s", "custom": { "axisLabel": "GC pause (s/s)" } } },
      "options": { "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }, "legend": { "displayMode": "table", "placement": "bottom", "calcs": ["mean", "max"] } }
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "JMeter child — GC pause time (rate, young vs old)",
      "description": "rate of the cumulative JMeter GC pause counters, converted ms→s (÷1000) so the Y axis matches the orchestrator GC panel exactly (GC pause seconds per second). A climbing OLD-gen pause rate over a long run is the classic 'JMeter is about to OOM' signal. 'No data' between runs.",
      "gridPos": { "x": 12, "y": 14, "w": 12, "h": 8 },
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "maxDataPoints": 500,
      "targets": [
        { "refId": "A", "expr": "sum by (instance) (rate(jmeter_jvm_gc_young_pause_ms{role=\"localOrchestrator\",instance=~\"$pod\"}[$__rate_interval])) / 1000", "legendFormat": "{{instance}} young" },
        { "refId": "B", "expr": "sum by (instance) (rate(jmeter_jvm_gc_old_pause_ms{role=\"localOrchestrator\",instance=~\"$pod\"}[$__rate_interval])) / 1000", "legendFormat": "{{instance}} old" }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "s", "custom": { "axisLabel": "GC pause (s/s)" } } },
      "options": { "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }, "legend": { "displayMode": "table", "placement": "bottom", "calcs": ["mean", "max"] } }
    },

    {
      "id": 14,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Orchestrator — threads (live / daemon)",
      "gridPos": { "x": 0, "y": 22, "w": 12, "h": 8 },
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "maxDataPoints": 500,
      "targets": [
        { "refId": "A", "expr": "jvm_threads_live_threads{role=\"localOrchestrator\",instance=~\"$pod\"}", "legendFormat": "{{instance}} live" },
        { "refId": "B", "expr": "jvm_threads_daemon_threads{role=\"localOrchestrator\",instance=~\"$pod\"}", "legendFormat": "{{instance}} daemon" }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "short", "custom": { "axisLabel": "Threads" } } },
      "options": { "tooltip": { "mode": "multi" }, "legend": { "displayMode": "table", "placement": "bottom", "calcs": ["mean", "lastNotNull"] } }
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "JMeter child — threads",
      "description": "jmeter_jvm_threads — tracks the configured thread-group size + JMeter's own pool. A runaway climb (threads never released) is a leak in the plan or the SUT keeping connections open. 'No data' between runs.",
      "gridPos": { "x": 12, "y": 22, "w": 12, "h": 8 },
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "maxDataPoints": 500,
      "targets": [
        { "refId": "A", "expr": "jmeter_jvm_threads{role=\"localOrchestrator\",instance=~\"$pod\"}", "legendFormat": "{{instance}}" }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "short", "custom": { "axisLabel": "Threads" } } },
      "options": { "tooltip": { "mode": "multi" }, "legend": { "displayMode": "table", "placement": "bottom", "calcs": ["mean", "max", "lastNotNull"] } }
    },

    {
      "id": 16,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "CPU % — orchestrator vs JMeter child",
      "description": "Orchestrator process_cpu_usage (×100) vs jmeter_jvm_cpu_percent on the same axis. The orchestrator hot path is single-threaded and should sit low (< a few %); JMeter is the CPU-heavy load generator. If the ORCHESTRATOR line climbs, the streaming pipeline is the bottleneck. JMeter line is 'No data' between runs.",
      "gridPos": { "x": 0, "y": 30, "w": 12, "h": 8 },
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "maxDataPoints": 500,
      "targets": [
        { "refId": "A", "expr": "100 * process_cpu_usage{role=\"localOrchestrator\",instance=~\"$pod\"}", "legendFormat": "{{instance}} orchestrator" },
        { "refId": "B", "expr": "jmeter_jvm_cpu_percent{role=\"localOrchestrator\",instance=~\"$pod\"}", "legendFormat": "{{instance}} jmeter" }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "percent", "min": 0 } },
      "options": { "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }, "legend": { "displayMode": "table", "placement": "bottom", "calcs": ["mean", "max"] } }
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Classes loaded — orchestrator vs JMeter child",
      "description": "Both should climb during warm-up then plateau. Continued growth = a class-loader leak (e.g. a JMeter plan compiling Groovy per sample). JMeter line is 'No data' between runs.",
      "gridPos": { "x": 12, "y": 30, "w": 12, "h": 8 },
      "datasource": "Prometheus",
      "maxDataPoints": 500,
      "targets": [
        { "refId": "A", "expr": "jvm_classes_loaded_classes{role=\"localOrchestrator\",instance=~\"$pod\"}", "legendFormat": "{{instance}} orchestrator" },
        { "refId": "B", "expr": "jmeter_jvm_classes_loaded{role=\"localOrchestrator\",instance=~\"$pod\"}", "legendFormat": "{{instance}} jmeter" }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "short" } },
      "options": { "tooltip": { "mode": "multi" }, "legend": { "displayMode": "table", "placement": "bottom", "calcs": ["lastNotNull"] } }
    }
  ]
}
